# Example environment file for this project.
#
# How to use:
#   1. Copy this file and name the copy ".env" (in the same folder: POCs).
#        cmd:        copy .env.example .env
#        PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env
#   2. Replace the placeholder values below with your own.
#   3. Restart Uvicorn (the .env file is only read at start-up).
#
# .env is listed in .gitignore, so your real password never goes to Git.
# This .env.example file IS committed, so it must never contain real secrets.
#
# Format:
#   postgresql+psycopg://<user>:<password>@<host>:<port>/<database>
#     postgresql+psycopg  database type + driver (psycopg 3)
#     <user>              PostgreSQL login the app uses
#     <password>          that user's password (URL-encoded, see below)
#     <host>              localhost = PostgreSQL runs on this computer
#     <port>              5432 = PostgreSQL's default port
#     <database>          database name
#
# If the password contains special characters, URL-encode them here:
#   @ -> %40    : -> %3A    / -> %2F    # -> %23    % -> %25
#   Example: password  pass@123  is written as  pass%40123
#
# Rules: one line per variable, no spaces around "=", no quotes.

DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://aiden_user:YOUR_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/aiden
